---
const rows = [65, 90, 115, 140];
---

<figure>
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 280 360"
    role="img"
    aria-label="Dois casos de junção de retalhos. No caso C1 as colunas P2, fronteira e Q1 estão igualmente espaçadas. No segundo caso, Q1 está ao dobro da distância e as derivadas transversais diferem."
  >
    <text x="140" y="24" text-anchor="middle">
      Derivadas iguais: C¹
    </text>
    {[60, 120, 180].map((x) => (
      <line x1={x} y1="65" x2={x} y2="140" class:list={{ seam: x === 120 }} />
    ))}
    {rows.map((y) => (
      <g>
        <line x1="60" y1={y} x2="180" y2={y} />
        {[60, 120, 180].map((x) => (
          <circle cx={x} cy={y} r="3" />
        ))}
      </g>
    ))}
    <text x="60" y="52" text-anchor="middle">
      P₂ⱼ
    </text>
    <text x="120" y="52" text-anchor="middle">
      P₃ⱼ = Q₀ⱼ
    </text>
    <text x="195" y="52" text-anchor="middle">
      Q₁ⱼ
    </text>
    <text x="90" y="164" text-anchor="middle">
      1
    </text>
    <text x="150" y="164" text-anchor="middle">
      1
    </text>
    <text x="140" y="204" text-anchor="middle">
      Mesmo plano tangente: G¹
    </text>
    {[60, 120, 240].map((x) => (
      <line x1={x} y1="245" x2={x} y2="320" class:list={{ seam: x === 120 }} />
    ))}
    {rows.map((y) => (
      <g>
        <line x1="60" y1={y + 180} x2="240" y2={y + 180} />
        {[60, 120, 240].map((x) => (
          <circle cx={x} cy={y + 180} r="3" />
        ))}
      </g>
    ))}
    <text x="60" y="232" text-anchor="middle">
      P₂ⱼ
    </text>
    <text x="120" y="232" text-anchor="middle">
      P₃ⱼ = Q₀ⱼ
    </text>
    <text x="240" y="232" text-anchor="middle">
      Q₁ⱼ
    </text>
    <text x="90" y="344" text-anchor="middle">
      1
    </text>
    <text x="180" y="344" text-anchor="middle">
      2
    </text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    A linha espessa é a fronteira comum. Mostram-se só as colunas que determinam
    a derivada transversal. Os restantes controlos continuam necessários para
    definir cada retalho.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  figure {
    margin: 24px 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 420px;
    height: auto;
    margin: auto;
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  text {
    fill: currentColor;
    font: 14px sans-serif;
  }
  line {
    stroke: var(--text);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .seam {
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 3;
  }
  circle {
    fill: var(--accent);
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
</style>
